27627945 [gemini-3.7-flash] #To implement a reliable buffer for timestamped GPIO states, several architectural considerations
27627945 [gemini-3.7-flash] #can help ensure the sampling remains fast and deterministic:
27627945 [gemini-3.7-flash] #
27627945 [gemini-3.7-flash] #1. Buffer Architecture (Fixed-Size Ring Buffer)
27627946 [gemini-3.7-flash] #• Pre-allocation: Dynamic containers like `std::vector` or `std::queue` can trigger heap
27627946 [gemini-3.7-flash] #reallocations during runtime, which introduces non-deterministic delays. A pre-allocated circular
27627946 [gemini-3.7-flash] #buffer (ring buffer) avoids dynamic memory overhead.
27627946 [gemini-3.7-flash] #• Element Layout: Storing the sample as a pair of 32-bit unsigned integers (`timestamp` and
27627947 [gemini-3.7-flash] #`pins`) creates an 8-byte record, fitting cleanly into standard alignment boundaries.
27627947 [gemini-3.7-flash] #
27627947 [gemini-3.7-flash] #2. Timing and Polling Latency
27627947 [gemini-3.7-flash] #• `sleep_us(100)` Impact: Sleeping for 100 microseconds inside the change-detection loop
27627948 [gemini-3.7-flash] #limits the maximum sampling frequency to roughly 10 kHz. For fast bus transactions (such as ROM
27627948 [gemini-3.7-flash] #accesses, which often complete in tens to hundreds of nanoseconds), polling without delay, using
27627948 [gemini-3.7-flash] #GPIO interrupt handlers, or using the RP2040 PIO (Programmable I/O) hardware will yield
27627948 [gemini-3.7-flash] #significantly higher fidelity.
27627949 [gemini-3.7-flash] #• Timestamp Rollover: A 32-bit microsecond counter (`t32`) overflows after approximately
27627949 [gemini-3.7-flash] #71.58 minutes. If long captures are required, either store the full 64-bit timestamp or handle the
27627949 [gemini-3.7-flash] #32-bit delta rollover in the consumer logic.
27627949 [gemini-3.7-flash] #
2762794a [gemini-3.7-flash] #3. Concurrency and Data Transfer
2762794a [gemini-3.7-flash] #• Lock-Free Sharing: If one core captures the pin states while the other core processes or
2762794a [gemini-3.7-flash] #transmits the buffer, a single-producer single-consumer (SPSC) lock-free ring buffer using atomic
2762794a [gemini-3.7-flash] #head and tail pointers avoids mutex contention.
2762794b [gemini-3.7-flash] #• Overflow Handling: Decide whether new samples should be dropped or if older unread
2762794b [gemini-3.7-flash] #samples should be overwritten when the buffer reaches capacity.
2762794b [gemini-3.7-flash] #
