27699f09 [nitro@ryzen5] pico_enable_stdio_usb(romulon 1) is needed for pico for me to use cdc commands to use usb coms?
27699f71 [gemini-3.7-flash] #🟠nitrologic Relay 2.0.2 gemini-3.7-flash 🌟 🪠 0.7° $0.003 560B 6.00s
27699f71 [gemini-3.7-flash] #Yes, that is correct.
27699f72 [gemini-3.7-flash] #
27699f72 [gemini-3.7-flash] #In your `CMakeLists.txt` file, calling `pico_enable_stdio_usb(romulon 1)` configures the Pico SDK
27699f72 [gemini-3.7-flash] #to route standard input and output (such as `printf` and `getchar`) over the USB CDC ACM (serial
27699f72 [gemini-3.7-flash] #COM) interface for your target (`romulon`).
27699f73 [gemini-3.7-flash] #
27699f73 [gemini-3.7-flash] #A few related points to keep in mind:
27699f73 [gemini-3.7-flash] #
27699f73 [gemini-3.7-flash] #• Disabling UART (Optional): By default, standard output also routes to the default
27699f74 [gemini-3.7-flash] #hardware UART pins. If you only want USB output and wish to disable the UART output, you can add
27699f74 [gemini-3.7-flash] #`pico_enable_stdio_uart(romulon 0)`.
27699f74 [gemini-3.7-flash] #• Initialization: In your C/C++ source file, you still need to call `stdio_init_all()` at
27699f74 [gemini-3.7-flash] #the beginning of your `main()` function to initialize the USB hardware and CDC stack.
27699f75 [gemini-3.7-flash] #• Direct TinyUSB Usage: If you plan to manage raw USB endpoints directly with the TinyUSB
27699f75 [gemini-3.7-flash] #library rather than using standard C library I/O, you would configure TinyUSB explicitly instead,
27699f75 [gemini-3.7-flash] #but for standard serial communication over COM ports, using `pico_enable_stdio_usb` is the standard
27699f75 [gemini-3.7-flash] #and recommended approach.
27699f76 [gemini-3.7-flash] #
2769a39e [nitro@ryzen5] pico_enable_stdio_usb(romulon 1)pico_enable_stdio_uart(romulon 0)
2769a3d7 [gemini-3.7-flash] #🟠nitrologic Relay 2.0.2 gemini-3.7-flash 🌟 🪠 0.7° $0.002 1.861KB 3.14s
2769a3d7 [gemini-3.7-flash] #That combination is the standard way to configure your Raspberry Pi Pico project to use only the
2769a3d8 [gemini-3.7-flash] #USB serial port while disabling hardware UART output.
2769a3d8 [gemini-3.7-flash] #
2769a3d8 [gemini-3.7-flash] #Just ensure that in your `CMakeLists.txt` file, the two commands are placed on separate lines (or
