2769c06e [gemini-3.7-flash] #The RP2040 is well-suited for this type of retrocomputing bus snooper.
2769c06f [gemini-3.7-flash] #
2769c06f [gemini-3.7-flash] #Between the high GPIO count, fast system clock, and the Programmable I/O (PIO) state machines, it
2769c06f [gemini-3.7-flash] #can sample address, data, and control lines (such as \Phi_2 and R/\overline\textW) synchronously
2769c06f [gemini-3.7-flash] #with minimal CPU overhead.
2769c070 [gemini-3.7-flash] #
2769c070 [gemini-3.7-flash] #The capture trace shows clean cycle tracking:
2769c070 [gemini-3.7-flash] #• The 16-bit address and 8-bit data lines are aligned correctly on instruction boundaries.
2769c070 [gemini-3.7-flash] #• The PIO/DMA pipeline is keeping up with the rapid back-to-back bus cycles of the inner `ADC #$01`
2769c071 [gemini-3.7-flash] #/ `BNE` loop without dropping cycles or corrupting the stream.
2769c071 [gemini-3.7-flash] #• Streaming the captured frames packaged as JSON-RPC over the RP2040's native USB CDC interface
2769c071 [gemini-3.7-flash] #provides a straightforward bridge to a host computer for real-time analysis.
2769c071 [gemini-3.7-flash] #
