27774da7 [gemini-3.7-flash] #Thank you for sharing `romulon.cpp`. Here is a review of the implementation and a few observations
27774da8 [gemini-3.7-flash] #regarding the logic, protocol formatting, and Pico SDK interactions:
27774da8 [gemini-3.7-flash] #
27774da8 [gemini-3.7-flash] #Key Observations
27774da8 [gemini-3.7-flash] #
27774da9 [gemini-3.7-flash] #1. JSON-RPC Response Formatting (`rpcSend`)
27774da9 [gemini-3.7-flash] #   * In `rpcSend`, the string construction outputs `"result":"<name>"="<value>"`. In standard JSON,
27774da9 [gemini-3.7-flash] #this structure produces invalid syntax due to the unescaped `=` operator between key-value pairs
27774da9 [gemini-3.7-flash] #inside a string or object. If the intention is to return an object or key-value mapping, formatting
27774da9 [gemini-3.7-flash] #it as a nested JSON object or a standard string value would avoid parser errors on the client side.
27774daa [gemini-3.7-flash] #
27774daa [gemini-3.7-flash] #2. Buffer Initialization in `pinStamp`
27774daa [gemini-3.7-flash] #   * `char buffer[20] = {32};` initializes the first element to ASCII space (`0x20`) and
27774daa [gemini-3.7-flash] #zero-initializes the remaining 19 elements. Since several explicit space assignments exist (indices
27774dab [gemini-3.7-flash] #5, 8, 10, 12), any index left untouched before index 17 might contain null terminators (`\0`) if
27774dab [gemini-3.7-flash] #not explicitly populated by `hexout`.
27774dab [gemini-3.7-flash] #
27774dab [gemini-3.7-flash] #3. Bus Decoding & Pin Shifting
27774dab [gemini-3.7-flash] #   * The bit-reversal and address line reconstruction in `pinStamp` effectively reorders the
27774dac [gemini-3.7-flash] #non-contiguous GPIO lines mapped to the 6502 address bus (A_0–A_15) and data bus (D_0–D_7).
27774dac [gemini-3.7-flash] #   * In `sampleRom` and `runShell`, operations mask certain high/floating lines. Note that reading
27774dac [gemini-3.7-flash] #floating inputs without internal pull-ups/pull-downs can cause jitter in polling loops if those
27774dac [gemini-3.7-flash] #lines are left unconnected.
27774dac [gemini-3.7-flash] #
27774dad [gemini-3.7-flash] #4. Timing and Sampling Precision
27774dad [gemini-3.7-flash] #   * In `sampleRom` and `runSample`, polling is throttled with `sleep_us(100)`. For high-speed bus
27774dad [gemini-3.7-flash] #sniffing (such as a 1 MHz or 2 MHz 6502 bus where cycle times are 500 ns–1000 ns), software polling
27774dad [gemini-3.7-flash] #with millisecond/microsecond sleeps will miss bus transactions. If higher precision capture is
27774dae [gemini-3.7-flash] #needed, the RP2040 PIO (Programmable I/O) hardware with DMA can sample pins cycle-accurately
27774dae [gemini-3.7-flash] #without CPU overhead.
27774dae [gemini-3.7-flash] #
27774dae [gemini-3.7-flash] #5. External Declarations and Linkage
27774daf [gemini-3.7-flash] #   * The code references several external identifiers (e.g., `out`, `hexout`, `cdcReadLine`,
27774daf [gemini-3.7-flash] #`cdcFlush`, `cdcInit`, `readBootSelect`, `rom_reset_usb_boot`, and `PICO_NVM`). These will need
27774daf [gemini-3.7-flash] #corresponding header definitions and linkage with the TinyUSB/Pico SDK libraries during the build.
27774daf [gemini-3.7-flash] #
27774daf [gemini-3.7-flash] #Please let me know if you would like targeted refactoring, PIO sampling suggestions, or adjustments
27774db0 [gemini-3.7-flash] #to any of these routines.
27774db0 [gemini-3.7-flash] #
27774ea7 [gemini-3.7-flash] #🟠nitrologic Relay 2.0.2 gemini-3.7-flash 🌟 🪠 0.7° $0.028 69.89KB 8.82s
27774ea7 [gemini-3.7-flash] #The log trace provides clear visibility into the system's runtime behavior. Here are the key
27774ea7 [gemini-3.7-flash] #observations from the captured session:
27774ea7 [gemini-3.7-flash] #
27774ea7 [gemini-3.7-flash] #1. 6502 RAM Initialization Sequence
27774ea8 [gemini-3.7-flash] #The bus captures starting around ID `200029` show a standard 6502 microprocessor reset/startup
27774ea8 [gemini-3.7-flash] #memory clearance and RAM sizing routine:
27774ea8 [gemini-3.7-flash] #• Loop execution in ROM (`EAAC`–`EAB2`):
27774ea8 [gemini-3.7-flash] #  * `$EAAC: 8A` (`TXA`)
27774ea9 [gemini-3.7-flash] #  * `EAAD: 95 00` (`STA 00,X` — writing accumulator values to zero-page addresses like `0014`,
27774ea9 [gemini-3.7-flash] #`008B`, `$00EF`)
27774ea9 [gemini-3.7-flash] #  * `$EAAF: E8` (`INX`)
