27775f72 [gemini-3.7-flash] #Analysis of the Sampled Bus State
27775f72 [gemini-3.7-flash] #• Address (`EA82`): The 6502 is executing code in the high ROM region (Commodore KERNAL /
27775f72 [gemini-3.7-flash] #BASIC startup area). `EA82` is part of the standard C64/VIC-20 initialization routine (specifically
27775f73 [gemini-3.7-flash] #initializing I/O vectors and clearing decimal mode).
27775f73 [gemini-3.7-flash] #• Data (`F4`): Read from address `EA82` (low byte of vector or opcode byte depending on the
27775f73 [gemini-3.7-flash] #specific KERNAL routine).
27775f74 [gemini-3.7-flash] #• R/W (`R`): Read operation (`RW` pin high / 1).
27775f74 [gemini-3.7-flash] #• CS (`1`): ROM select line is active (decoded as active-high representation in your
27775f74 [gemini-3.7-flash] #formatter).
27775f74 [gemini-3.7-flash] #• Timestamp (`$DBA9`): 56,233 µs mark.
27775f74 [gemini-3.7-flash] #
27775f75 [gemini-3.7-flash] #Minor Detail
27775f75 [gemini-3.7-flash] #• The column header still contains the three 's' characters in `"Addresss"`. If your host-side
27775f75 [gemini-3.7-flash] #parser expects standard spelling, updating the string literal in the firmware from `"Addresss Data
27775f75 [gemini-3.7-flash] #CS RW T"` to `"Address Data CS RW T"` will keep it clean.
