27776180 [gemini-3.7-flash] #🟠nitrologic Relay 2.0.2 gemini-3.7-flash 🌟 🪠 0.7° $0.023 75.04KB 6.74s
27776180 [gemini-3.7-flash] #Understood. When reverse-engineering or bringing up custom hardware, address and data line swapping
27776180 [gemini-3.7-flash] #is very common.
27776181 [gemini-3.7-flash] #
27776181 [gemini-3.7-flash] #Looking at your captured trace, there are a few clues we can use to verify or detect pin
27776181 [gemini-3.7-flash] #permutations:
27776181 [gemini-3.7-flash] #
27776182 [gemini-3.7-flash] #1. The RAM Sizing Loop Signature
27776182 [gemini-3.7-flash] #In your earlier trace, we see this repeating write pattern:
27776182 [gemini-3.7-flash] #• Cycle 1: `0000 13 R` / `0000 25 W` / `0000 2f W`
27776182 [gemini-3.7-flash] #• Cycle 2: `0000 77 R` / `0000 b0 W` / `0000 b9 W`
27776183 [gemini-3.7-flash] #• Cycle 3: `0001 40 R` / `0001 49 W` / `0001 52 W`
27776183 [gemini-3.7-flash] #• Cycle 4: `0001 a4 R` / `0001 ad W` / `0001 b6 W`
27776183 [gemini-3.7-flash] #• Cycle 5: `0002 3d R` / `0002 46 W` / `0002 4f W`
27776183 [gemini-3.7-flash] #
27776183 [gemini-3.7-flash] #• Notice:*
27776184 [gemini-3.7-flash] #• The address increments: `0000` \rightarrow `0001` \rightarrow `0002` \rightarrow ... \rightarrow
27776184 [gemini-3.7-flash] #`0011`.
27776184 [gemini-3.7-flash] #• The write values advance by roughly consistent deltas:
27776184 [gemini-3.7-flash] #  * `49 - 40 = 9`
27776184 [gemini-3.7-flash] #  * `52 - 49 = 9`
27776185 [gemini-3.7-flash] #  * `AD - A4 = 9`
27776185 [gemini-3.7-flash] #  * `B6 - AD = 9`
27776185 [gemini-3.7-flash] #• Because the address values and data steps increment cleanly in order, A_0–A_7, A_8–A_15, and
27776185 [gemini-3.7-flash] #D_0–D_7 are already substantially correct. If data or address bits were swapped out of order,
27776186 [gemini-3.7-flash] #you would see erratic, non-monotonic jumps in those increments.
27776186 [gemini-3.7-flash] #
27776186 [gemini-3.7-flash] #━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━
27776186 [gemini-3.7-flash] #
27776187 [gemini-3.7-flash] #2. Spot-Checking Pin Mappings
27776187 [gemini-3.7-flash] #
27776187 [gemini-3.7-flash] #If any lines still seem suspect, here are straightforward ways to confirm individual pin groups:
27776187 [gemini-3.7-flash] #
27776188 [gemini-3.7-flash] #1. Address Lines (A_0–A_15):
27776188 [gemini-3.7-flash] #   * Watch the lower byte during consecutive opcode fetches (e.g., `eaaf`, `eab0`, `eab1`, `eab2`).
27776188 [gemini-3.7-flash] #If A_0 or A_1 were swapped or inverted, the sequence would not increment consecutively (`+1`).
27776188 [gemini-3.7-flash] #   * Watch the upper address byte during page crossing (e.g., transitioning from `00FF` to `0100`).
27776189 [gemini-3.7-flash] #
27776189 [gemini-3.7-flash] #2. Data Lines (D_0–D_7):
27776189 [gemini-3.7-flash] #   * Compare fetched opcodes with the standard 6502 instruction set. For instance:
27776189 [gemini-3.7-flash] #     * `$E8` = `INX` (Binary `1110 1000`)
27776189 [gemini-3.7-flash] #     * `$D0` = `BNE` (Binary `1101 0000`)
2777618a [gemini-3.7-flash] #     * `$8A` = `TXA` (Binary `1000 1010`)
2777618a [gemini-3.7-flash] #     * `$95` = `STA zpg,X` (Binary `1001 0101`)
2777618a [gemini-3.7-flash] #   * Since these exact opcodes appear in valid functional sequence around `EAAC`–`EAB2`, your `d =
2777618b [gemini-3.7-flash] #(pins >> 13) & 0xff` mapping and bit ordering match the actual hardware.
2777618b [gemini-3.7-flash] #
2777618b [gemini-3.7-flash] #3. R/W and CS Lines:
2777618b [gemini-3.7-flash] #   * Writes (`W`) only happen when accessing RAM/I/O addresses (`0000`–`07FF`), and opcode fetches
2777618b [gemini-3.7-flash] #from ROM (`EAxx`) are always Reads (`R`), confirming the R/\overline{W}$ pin mask `0x10000000` is
2777618c [gemini-3.7-flash] #assigned to the correct polarity.
2777618c [gemini-3.7-flash] #
2777618c [gemini-3.7-flash] #If you observe any unexpected address jumps or invalid opcodes later in the trace, let me know and
2777618c [gemini-3.7-flash] #we can isolate the specific bit shifts.
2777618d [gemini-3.7-flash] #
