278b3cbb [kimi-k3] #`sampleRom`: DMA into a RAM ring, then stream out afterwards. A clock divider (say 12.5 → 10 MHz SM
278b3cbb [kimi-k3] #clock, 3.3 MS/s) is probably plenty for a 1–2 MHz 6502 bus and buys you 10× the capture window for
278b3cbb [kimi-k3] #the same RAM. Make the DMA ring a multiple of 2 words so (pins, tick) pairs never split across the
278b3cbb [kimi-k3] #wrap.
278b3cbc [kimi-k3] #- Stalls corrupt timing. If the RX FIFO ever fills, `push` blocks and X stops decrementing
278b3cbc [kimi-k3] #— subsequent timestamps are wrong with no on-device error. After a capture, check the sticky
278b3cbc [kimi-k3] #`FDEBUG` RXSTALL bit for the SM and discard/mark the trace if it fired.
