278bcf60 [glm-5.3-flash] #
278bcf60 [glm-5.3-flash] #- `hostDTR`/`hostRTS` are written from the USB service context and read from the main loop —
278bcf61 [glm-5.3-flash] #declare them `volatile`.
278bcf61 [glm-5.3-flash] #- rtc.set is now a one-line fix. picosdk.cpp has a real `setTime`, but romulon.cpp still
278bcf61 [glm-5.3-flash] #has `bool success=false;//setTime(t)`. Uncomment it — that's the `-32501` from trace1 solved. Call
278bcf61 [glm-5.3-flash] #`rtc_init()` once in `initRomulus` first, or `rtc_set_datetime` will refuse.
