278e74dc [grok-build-0.1] #
278e74dc [grok-build-0.1] #The core problem (recap)
278e74dc [grok-build-0.1] #
278e74dc [grok-build-0.1] #`transfer_count` counts down from the number you requested.
278e74dd [grok-build-0.1] #Right now your function returns the remaining amount.
278e74dd [grok-build-0.1] #
278e74dd [grok-build-0.1] #You want the opposite: how many transfers have actually been completed (i.e. "value
278e74dd [grok-build-0.1] #transmitted").
278e74de [grok-build-0.1] #
278e74de [grok-build-0.1] #How to fix it
278e74de [grok-build-0.1] #
278e74de [grok-build-0.1] #You need to do two things:
278e74df [grok-build-0.1] #
278e74df [grok-build-0.1] #1. Remember the original number of transfers when you start the capture.
278e74df [grok-build-0.1] #2. Calculate:
278e74df [grok-build-0.1] #   `captured = (original_requested - current_transfer_count) / 2`
278e74e0 [grok-build-0.1] #
