278e74e0 [grok-build-0.1] #
278e74e0 [grok-build-0.1] #What needs to change
278e74e1 [grok-build-0.1] #
278e74e1 [grok-build-0.1] #You will need to:
278e74e1 [grok-build-0.1] #
278e74e1 [grok-build-0.1] #- Add a static variable that stores the original transfer count.
278e74e2 [grok-build-0.1] #- Save that value inside `startBusCapture()`.
278e74e2 [grok-build-0.1] #- Change `getCapturedSampleCount()` (your `snoopCount`) to return `(original - current) / 2`.
278e74e2 [grok-build-0.1] #
278e74e2 [grok-build-0.1] #Important details
278e74e3 [grok-build-0.1] #
278e74e3 [grok-build-0.1] #- The value should be in samples (not words), so divide by 2 at the end.
278e74e3 [grok-build-0.1] #- You should handle the case where `transfer_count` temporarily reads higher than the original due
278e74e3 [grok-build-0.1] #to DMA timing (use a clamp).
278e74e4 [grok-build-0.1] #- After the transfer finishes, the result should equal the number of samples you requested.
