278e9a7f [grok-build-0.1] #• Yes*, the order is currently correct.
278e9a7f [grok-build-0.1] #
278e9a80 [grok-build-0.1] #Current situation:
278e9a80 [grok-build-0.1] #
278e9a80 [grok-build-0.1] #In the PIO program (`snoop.pio`), when a change is detected, it does this:
278e9a80 [grok-build-0.1] #
278e9a81 [grok-build-0.1] #
278e9a81 [grok-build-0.1] #push      ; pushes tick first
278e9a81 [grok-build-0.1] #push      ; pushes pins second
278e9a81 [grok-build-0.1] #
278e9a82 [grok-build-0.1] #
278e9a82 [grok-build-0.1] #So every pair that comes out of the PIO FIFO is in this order:
278e9a82 [grok-build-0.1] #
278e9a82 [grok-build-0.1] #- First word → tick (time value)
278e9a83 [grok-build-0.1] #- Second word → pins
278e9a83 [grok-build-0.1] #
278e9a83 [grok-build-0.1] #Your code respects this:
278e9a83 [grok-build-0.1] #
278e9a84 [grok-build-0.1] #
278e9a84 [grok-build-0.1] #uint32_t tick  = captureBuffer[i * 2];      // even = tick
278e9a84 [grok-build-0.1] #uint32_t pins  = captureBuffer[i * 2 + 1];  // odd  = pins
278e9a84 [grok-build-0.1] #
278e9a85 [grok-build-0.1] #
278e9a85 [grok-build-0.1] #This matches the order the PIO is pushing.
278e9a85 [grok-build-0.1] #
278e9a85 [grok-build-0.1] #━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━
278e9a86 [grok-build-0.1] #
278e9a86 [grok-build-0.1] #Important caveat:
278e9a86 [grok-build-0.1] #
278e9a86 [grok-build-0.1] #Even though the order is correct, the `tick` value itself is not a real timestamp.
278e9a87 [grok-build-0.1] #It is a countdown value from the PIO (it starts at 0xFFFFFFFF and counts down between changes).
278e9a87 [grok-build-0.1] #
278e9a87 [grok-build-0.1] #So while the pairing is right, the actual time values you're getting are still not useful for
278e9a87 [grok-build-0.1] #timing analysis.
278e9a88 [grok-build-0.1] #
278e9a88 [grok-build-0.1] #Would you like to look at fixing the timestamp quality next, or is there something else about the
278e9a88 [grok-build-0.1] #ordering you're unsure about?
278e9a88 [grok-build-0.1] #
