27a11b18 [grok-build-0.1] #The main issue right now is a runaway echo loop combined with very heavy logging. This is
27a11b18 [grok-build-0.1] #why Godot crashes with "output overflow" and then forcibly closes the connection (error 10054).
27a11b19 [grok-build-0.1] #
27a11b19 [grok-build-0.1] #What’s happening:
27a11b19 [grok-build-0.1] #
27a11b19 [grok-build-0.1] #1. Your TypeScript client sends `"tick"`.
27a11b1a [grok-build-0.1] #2. Godot receives it and always sends a big response back (with the full original message
27a11b1a [grok-build-0.1] #inside).
27a11b1a [grok-build-0.1] #3. The client’s `onMessage` then does `this.send("echo", {payload})` on every message.
27a11b1a [grok-build-0.1] #4. This creates deeply nested JSON that keeps growing.
27a11b1b [grok-build-0.1] #5. `glog()` prints the entire massive string every time → output overflows → crash.
