27a1853c [grok-build-0.1] #• Good, let's keep this as discussion only.*
27a1853c [grok-build-0.1] #
27a1853c [grok-build-0.1] #Here are the things I think are currently most important to consider, ranked roughly by impact:
27a1853d [grok-build-0.1] #
27a1853d [grok-build-0.1] #1. Root Node Choice (Very Important Right Now)
27a1853d [grok-build-0.1] #Your current root is a `Control`. This is fine for pure UI and logging, but it creates friction the
27a1853d [grok-build-0.1] #moment you want to spawn 3D content (GLBs).
27a1853e [grok-build-0.1] #
27a1853e [grok-build-0.1] #- 3D nodes added under a `Control` will not render by default.
27a1853e [grok-build-0.1] #- You will need some kind of bridge (SubViewport, separate 3D scene, or changing the root
27a1853e [grok-build-0.1] #structure) to actually see the models.
27a1853f [grok-build-0.1] #- This decision affects how clean your scene hierarchy stays as the project grows.
27a1853f [grok-build-0.1] #
27a1853f [grok-build-0.1] #• Question: How important is it that you can see* the spawned GLBs in the near
27a1853f [grok-build-0.1] #future?
27a18540 [grok-build-0.1] #
27a18540 [grok-build-0.1] #2. Logging Discipline
27a18540 [grok-build-0.1] #You've already run into output overflow and connection drops caused by excessive logging.
27a18540 [grok-build-0.1] #
27a18541 [grok-build-0.1] #Even if it feels harmless now, logging every incoming message (especially high-frequency ones like
27a18541 [grok-build-0.1] #`tick`) becomes a serious liability. It affects:
27a18541 [grok-build-0.1] #- Performance
27a18541 [grok-build-0.1] #- Readability of logs
27a18542 [grok-build-0.1] #- Connection stability
27a18542 [grok-build-0.1] #
27a18542 [grok-build-0.1] #This is one of the easiest things to get wrong early.
27a18542 [grok-build-0.1] #
27a18543 [grok-build-0.1] #3. Message Semantics (Request vs Notification)
27a18543 [grok-build-0.1] #You're using JSON-RPC, but not all messages need a response.
27a18543 [grok-build-0.1] #
27a18543 [grok-build-0.1] #- `tick` looks like a heartbeat or state update. Does it really need any reply?
27a18544 [grok-build-0.1] #- `spawn` probably does need some form of feedback (success/failure).
27a18544 [grok-build-0.1] #- Over-responding creates noise and potential loops.
27a18544 [grok-build-0.1] #
27a18544 [grok-build-0.1] #Think about which messages are commands vs state updates.
27a18545 [grok-build-0.1] #
27a18545 [grok-build-0.1] #4. Connection Reality vs Intent
27a18545 [grok-build-0.1] #Your script still tries to connect upstream to port 9000 on every run, even though nothing appears
27a18545 [grok-build-0.1] #to be there.
27a18546 [grok-build-0.1] #
27a18546 [grok-build-0.1] #This raises a bigger question:
27a18546 [grok-build-0.1] #- Is the Godot side meant to be a client to something else (port 9000), or purely a
27a18546 [grok-build-0.1] #server for the TypeScript client?
27a18547 [grok-build-0.1] #- The current dual role (listening + connecting upstream) adds complexity and failure points.
27a18547 [grok-build-0.1] #
27a18547 [grok-build-0.1] #5. Separation of Concerns
27a18547 [grok-build-0.1] #Right now most logic lives in one `Node`. As you add spawning, different GLB handling, state
27a18548 [grok-build-0.1] #tracking, etc., this can get messy quickly.
27a18548 [grok-build-0.1] #
27a18548 [grok-build-0.1] #Worth thinking about early:
27a18548 [grok-build-0.1] #- Should networking stay isolated from scene creation?
27a18549 [grok-build-0.1] #- Do you want a central "command handler" or should things be more event-driven?
27a18549 [grok-build-0.1] #
27a18549 [grok-build-0.1] #6. Reliability Expectations
27a18549 [grok-build-0.1] #You asked about checksums and ACKs earlier. This is important to decide on now rather than later:
27a1854a [grok-build-0.1] #
27a1854a [grok-build-0.1] #- Are `tick` messages allowed to be lost?
27a1854a [grok-build-0.1] #- Do `spawn` commands need guaranteed delivery or at least confirmation?
27a1854a [grok-build-0.1] #- How much do you care about message ordering?
27a1854b [grok-build-0.1] #
27a1854b [grok-build-0.1] #WebSocket + JSON-RPC gives you very little of this for free.
27a1854b [grok-build-0.1] #
27a1854b [grok-build-0.1] #━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━
27a1854c [grok-build-0.1] #
27a1854c [grok-build-0.1] #What I would focus on first (if this were my project):
27a1854c [grok-build-0.1] #
