27a1be4f [grok-build-0.1] #🟠nitrologic Relay 2.0.2 grok-build-0.1 𝕏 🪠 0.7° $0.046 118.5KB 16.37s
27a1be4f [grok-build-0.1] #• Got it. For a simple, optimal, clean baseline* on a vector display peripheral,
27a1be50 [grok-build-0.1] #let's focus on what actually matters.
27a1be50 [grok-build-0.1] #
27a1be50 [grok-build-0.1] #Core Goal for Baseline
27a1be50 [grok-build-0.1] #You want the cleanest possible lines with the least complexity, as a solid foundation. This means
27a1be51 [grok-build-0.1] #prioritizing sharpness and anti-aliasing quality over effects, authenticity, or advanced
27a1be51 [grok-build-0.1] #features for now.
27a1be51 [grok-build-0.1] #
27a1be51 [grok-build-0.1] #Most Important Considerations Right Now
27a1be52 [grok-build-0.1] #
27a1be52 [grok-build-0.1] #• 1. 2D Canvas is the right domain*
27a1be52 [grok-build-0.1] #For pure vector lines (especially as a baseline), stay in 2D inside the SubViewport. Using 3D
27a1be52 [grok-build-0.1] #geometry or 3D line rendering adds unnecessary complexity and usually worse results for thin, clean
27a1be53 [grok-build-0.1] #lines. Treat the vector display as a 2D canvas problem, even if the rest of your project mixes
27a1be53 [grok-build-0.1] #2D/3D.
27a1be53 [grok-build-0.1] #
27a1be53 [grok-build-0.1] #• 2. Line rendering method is the biggest quality lever*
27a1be54 [grok-build-0.1] #This is where most people lose cleanliness:
27a1be54 [grok-build-0.1] #
27a1be54 [grok-build-0.1] #- Standard `draw_line()` or default materials tend to look jagged or blurry when rendered to a
27a1be54 [grok-build-0.1] #texture.
27a1be55 [grok-build-0.1] #- `Line2D` nodes with `antialiased = true` can work surprisingly well as a baseline, but have
27a1be55 [grok-build-0.1] #limits (especially with many lines or very thin widths).
27a1be55 [grok-build-0.1] #- A simple custom canvas shader often becomes the "simple optimal" choice faster than expected,
27a1be55 [grok-build-0.1] #because it gives you direct control over anti-aliasing without much extra code complexity.
27a1be56 [grok-build-0.1] #
27a1be56 [grok-build-0.1] #For a clean baseline, you should decide early whether you're willing to use one lightweight shader
27a1be56 [grok-build-0.1] #for line drawing, or try to stay with built-in nodes.
27a1be56 [grok-build-0.1] #
27a1be57 [grok-build-0.1] #• 3. SubViewport + Texture Display Settings*
27a1be57 [grok-build-0.1] #Even with perfect line drawing, you can ruin the result at the display stage. Important factors:
27a1be57 [grok-build-0.1] #
27a1be57 [grok-build-0.1] #- The resolution of the SubViewport relative to how big it appears in the UI.
27a1be58 [grok-build-0.1] #- Texture filtering on the `TextureRect` (or `SubViewportContainer`) that shows the result.
27a1be58 [grok-build-0.1] #Filtering is often the enemy of crisp vector lines.
27a1be58 [grok-build-0.1] #- Whether the viewport itself uses any MSAA.
27a1be58 [grok-build-0.1] #- Pixel snapping behavior in the 2D canvas.
27a1be59 [grok-build-0.1] #
27a1be59 [grok-build-0.1] #For clean lines, you usually want the output texture to be sampled without linear filtering
27a1be59 [grok-build-0.1] #when possible.
27a1be59 [grok-build-0.1] #
27a1be5a [grok-build-0.1] #• 4. Coordinate Mapping and Precision*
27a1be5a [grok-build-0.1] #Since this is tied to a 6502 simulator:
27a1be5a [grok-build-0.1] #- How you map the simulator’s vector coordinates into the SubViewport space matters.
27a1be5a [grok-build-0.1] #- Floating point precision and snapping can destroy line quality.
27a1be5b [grok-build-0.1] #- You want a predictable, stable mapping that doesn’t introduce jitter or uneven line thickness.
27a1be5b [grok-build-0.1] #
27a1be5b [grok-build-0.1] #• 5. Batching and Redraw Strategy*
27a1be5b [grok-build-0.1] #For a baseline, keep the drawing model simple:
27a1be5c [grok-build-0.1] #- Are you clearing and redrawing all vectors every frame?
27a1be5c [grok-build-0.1] #- Or incrementally adding lines?
27a1be5c [grok-build-0.1] #
27a1be5c [grok-build-0.1] #The simpler and more consistent the redraw model, the easier it is to keep the rendering clean and
27a1be5d [grok-build-0.1] #predictable.
27a1be5d [grok-build-0.1] #
27a1be5d [grok-build-0.1] #• 6. What "Clean" Actually Means Here*
27a1be5d [grok-build-0.1] #For your baseline, define what good enough looks like:
27a1be5e [grok-build-0.1] #- Thin lines (1–2 pixels) that don’t look aliased or blurry.
27a1be5e [grok-build-0.1] #- Consistent thickness regardless of angle.
27a1be5e [grok-build-0.1] #- No visible stepping on diagonal lines.
27a1be5e [grok-build-0.1] #- Lines that remain sharp when the UI panel is at its normal size.
27a1be5f [grok-build-0.1] #
27a1be5f [grok-build-0.1] #Avoid chasing glow, brightness falloff, or phosphor effects until the baseline lines are solid.
27a1be5f [grok-build-0.1] #
27a1be5f [grok-build-0.1] #Recommended Thinking Order for Baseline
27a1be60 [grok-build-0.1] #
27a1be60 [grok-build-0.1] #1. Decide on drawing primitive — Start by evaluating whether `Line2D` nodes are sufficient,
27a1be60 [grok-build-0.1] #or whether a single custom material/shader for lines will be simpler long-term.
27a1be60 [grok-build-0.1] #2. Lock down the SubViewport setup — Resolution, MSAA, and how the texture is sampled in
27a1be61 [grok-build-0.1] #the UI.
27a1be61 [grok-build-0.1] #3. Control the final display — How the rendered texture is shown in your Control-based UI
27a1be61 [grok-build-0.1] #(filtering, scaling, etc.).
27a1be61 [grok-build-0.1] #4. Coordinate system — Make the mapping from simulator vectors to screen space as clean as
27a1be62 [grok-build-0.1] #possible.
27a1be62 [grok-build-0.1] #
27a1be62 [grok-build-0.1] #Trade-off to be aware of
27a1be62 [grok-build-0.1] #The absolute simplest approach (just using `Line2D` + MSAA) is fast to implement but often fails to
27a1be63 [grok-build-0.1] #stay "clean" once you have real vector data. A slightly more deliberate approach (lightweight line
27a1be63 [grok-build-0.1] #shader + careful texture settings) tends to give a much better baseline with only moderate extra
27a1be63 [grok-build-0.1] #effort.
27a1be63 [grok-build-0.1] #
27a1be64 [grok-build-0.1] #━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━
