27a1d912 [grok-build-0.1] #        "POSITION": 0,
27a1d912 [grok-build-0.1] #        "COLOR_0": 1     // optional: for brightness
27a1d912 [grok-build-0.1] #      }
27a1d913 [grok-build-0.1] #    }]
27a1d913 [grok-build-0.1] #  }]
27a1d913 [grok-build-0.1] #}
27a1d913 [grok-build-0.1] #
27a1d914 [grok-build-0.1] #
27a1d914 [grok-build-0.1] #• Buffer layout* (what you asked about):
27a1d914 [grok-build-0.1] #
27a1d914 [grok-build-0.1] #
27a1d915 [grok-build-0.1] #Buffer (binary):
27a1d915 [grok-build-0.1] #[ x1, y1, x2, y2, x3, y3, x4, y4, ... ]     // POSITION (VEC2)
27a1d915 [grok-build-0.1] #[ r1, g1, b1, a1, r2, g2, b2, a2, ... ]     // COLOR_0 (brightness as alpha or intensity)
27a1d915 [grok-build-0.1] #
27a1d916 [grok-build-0.1] #
27a1d916 [grok-build-0.1] #This is one of the cleanest ways to express raw line lists in glTF.
27a1d916 [grok-build-0.1] #
27a1d916 [grok-build-0.1] #Cleanliness Breakdown (Realistic)
27a1d917 [grok-build-0.1] #
27a1d917 [grok-build-0.1] #╭─────────────────────────────┬──────────────┬───────────────────────────────────────────────────╮
27a1d917 [grok-build-0.1] #│  Aspect                     │  Rating      │  Comments                                         │
27a1d917 [grok-build-0.1] #├─────────────────────────────┼──────────────┼───────────────────────────────────────────────────┤
27a1d918 [grok-build-0.1] #│  **Buffer for x,y**         │  Good        │  Simple VEC2 works cleanly                        │
27a1d918 [grok-build-0.1] #│  **Line semantics**         │  Acceptable  │  `mode: 1` (LINES) is the correct mode            │
27a1d918 [grok-build-0.1] #│  **Brightness**             │  Acceptable  │  Can ride along in `COLOR_0`                      │
27a1d918 [grok-build-0.1] #│  **Per-frame updates**      │  Poor        │  glTF is not designed for this                    │
27a1d919 [grok-build-0.1] #│  **Parsing overhead**       │  High        │  JSON + buffer parsing is heavy for small frames  │
27a1d919 [grok-build-0.1] #│  **Simplicity in Godot**    │  Low–Medium  │  Standard importer is too heavy for this          │
27a1d919 [grok-build-0.1] #│  **Standardization**        │  Excellent   │  This is the main win if glTF is first-class      │
27a1d919 [grok-build-0.1] #╰─────────────────────────────┴──────────────┴───────────────────────────────────────────────────╯
27a1d91a [grok-build-0.1] #
27a1d91a [grok-build-0.1] #Important Practical Considerations
27a1d91a [grok-build-0.1] #
27a1d91a [grok-build-0.1] #1. Don't use Godot's normal glTF importer per frame
27a1d91b [grok-build-0.1] #   - The built-in `load("res://...")` or `GLTFDocument` import path is far too slow and heavy for
27a1d91b [grok-build-0.1] #per-frame data.
27a1d91b [grok-build-0.1] #   - You would need to manually parse the glTF (or .glb) and extract the buffers yourself
27a1d91b [grok-build-0.1] #using `GLTFDocument` + `GLTFState` in a lightweight way, or parse the binary directly.
27a1d91c [grok-build-0.1] #
27a1d91c [grok-build-0.1] #2. JSON vs Binary (.glb)
27a1d91c [grok-build-0.1] #   - `.gltf` (JSON + separate buffer) = very chatty for small line lists.
27a1d91c [grok-build-0.1] #   - `.glb` (single binary) = much better, but still carries glTF metadata overhead (scenes, nodes,
27a1d91d [grok-build-0.1] #accessors, bufferViews, etc.).
27a1d91d [grok-build-0.1] #
27a1d91d [grok-build-0.1] #3. Coordinate System Friction
27a1d91d [grok-build-0.1] #   - glTF uses right-handed Y-up by default. For a 2D vector display you'll need to decide on a
27a1d91e [grok-build-0.1] #consistent mapping (and document it).
27a1d91e [grok-build-0.1] #   - Using `VEC2` in `POSITION` is allowed, but many tools and parts of the spec assume 3D.
27a1d91e [grok-build-0.1] #
27a1d91e [grok-build-0.1] #4. Future-Proofing vs Current Overhead
27a1d91f [grok-build-0.1] #   Since glTF is first-class in your design, the real question becomes:
27a1d91f [grok-build-0.1] #
27a1d91f [grok-build-0.1] #   - Are you willing to pay the parsing + structure cost now so that vector data, 3D models, and
27a1d91f [grok-build-0.1] #future assets all live in the same format?
27a1d920 [grok-build-0.1] #   - Or do you want a lighter custom format for the vector stream and only use glTF for
27a1d920 [grok-build-0.1] #static/heavier assets?
27a1d920 [grok-build-0.1] #
27a1d920 [grok-build-0.1] #Realistic Recommendation
27a1d921 [grok-build-0.1] #
27a1d921 [grok-build-0.1] #If glTF must be first-class, then the cleanest way forward is:
27a1d921 [grok-build-0.1] #
27a1d921 [grok-build-0.1] #- Send minimal .glb files (or raw glTF JSON + buffer) containing only a single mesh in
27a1d922 [grok-build-0.1] #`LINES` mode.
27a1d922 [grok-build-0.1] #- On the Godot side, write a small dedicated parser that extracts the `POSITION` and `COLOR_0`
27a1d922 [grok-build-0.1] #buffers directly, bypassing the full scene import.
27a1d922 [grok-build-0.1] #- Accept that there will be some structural overhead compared to a raw line list.
27a1d923 [grok-build-0.1] #
27a1d923 [grok-build-0.1] #This is doable, but it won't be as "simple" as sending a raw array of lines.
27a1d923 [grok-build-0.1] #
27a1d923 [grok-build-0.1] #━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━
27a1d924 [grok-build-0.1] #
27a1d924 [grok-build-0.1] #Questions to help decide the direction:
27a1d924 [grok-build-0.1] #
27a1d924 [grok-build-0.1] #1. Do you want to send one glTF per frame, or are you thinking of using glTF more as a
27a1d925 [grok-build-0.1] #schema/format definition while sending lighter binary data?
27a1d925 [grok-build-0.1] #
27a1d925 [grok-build-0.1] #2. How important is it that the same format can be used for both the vector display
27a1d925 [grok-build-0.1] #and regular 3D GLB models in the project?
27a1d926 [grok-build-0.1] #
27a1d926 [grok-build-0.1] #3. Are you okay with manually parsing the buffers in Godot, or do you want to stay within Godot’s
27a1d926 [grok-build-0.1] #standard glTF loading APIs?
27a1d926 [grok-build-0.1] #
27a1d927 [grok-build-0.1] #Let me know your leanings and I can go deeper into either the buffer layout details or the
27a1d927 [grok-build-0.1] #Godot-side parsing strategy.
27a1d927 [grok-build-0.1] #
