27a1fce9 [grok-build-0.1] #The issue is structural:
27a1fce9 [grok-build-0.1] #
27a1fcea [grok-build-0.1] #- `draw_line()` is a CanvasItem method. It only works inside `_draw()` (or via
27a1fcea [grok-build-0.1] #`queue_redraw()`).
27a1fcea [grok-build-0.1] #- Your node extends `Node`, which is not a `CanvasItem`.
27a1fcea [grok-build-0.1] #- Calling `draw_line()` from `onPacket()` (which runs during network polling) does nothing visible.
27a1fceb [grok-build-0.1] #
27a1fceb [grok-build-0.1] #Even if the conversion works, the lines are being "drawn" in a context that doesn't actually render
27a1fceb [grok-build-0.1] #to the screen.
27a1fceb [grok-build-0.1] #
27a1fcec [grok-build-0.1] #Other Issues
27a1fcec [grok-build-0.1] #
27a1fcec [grok-build-0.1] #- `draw()` is a bad name here because it conflicts with the concept of Godot's drawing system.
27a1fcec [grok-build-0.1] #- Logging the full base64 on every draw will get very noisy fast.
27a1fced [grok-build-0.1] #- You're treating the incoming message as having a direct `.buffer` field. With real glTF this
27a1fced [grok-build-0.1] #would be deeper in the structure (`meshes[0].primitives[0].attributes.POSITION` → accessor →
27a1fced [grok-build-0.1] #bufferView → buffer).
27a1fced [grok-build-0.1] #
