27a20e96 [grok-build-0.1] #Recommended Approach (Discussion)
27a20e96 [grok-build-0.1] #
27a20e97 [grok-build-0.1] #You should separate concerns like this:
27a20e97 [grok-build-0.1] #
27a20e97 [grok-build-0.1] #- `node.gd` (the `Node`):
27a20e97 [grok-build-0.1] #  - Handles networking
27a20e98 [grok-build-0.1] #  - Receives the `"draw"` message
27a20e98 [grok-build-0.1] #  - Stores the latest line data (as `PackedVector2Array`)
27a20e98 [grok-build-0.1] #  - Tells the `Node2D` when it should redraw
27a20e98 [grok-build-0.1] #
27a20e99 [grok-build-0.1] #- `node2d.gd` (the `Node2D`):
27a20e99 [grok-build-0.1] #  - Holds the current line data
27a20e99 [grok-build-0.1] #  - Does the actual drawing in `_draw()`
27a20e99 [grok-build-0.1] #  - Gets told to redraw via `queue_redraw()`
27a20e9a [grok-build-0.1] #
27a20e9a [grok-build-0.1] #This is the clean pattern in Godot for this kind of thing.
27a20e9a [grok-build-0.1] #
27a20e9a [grok-build-0.1] #Key Points to Consider
27a20e9b [grok-build-0.1] #
27a20e9b [grok-build-0.1] #- The networking node should not do any drawing logic.
27a20e9b [grok-build-0.1] #- When a `"draw"` message arrives, the networking node should:
27a20e9b [grok-build-0.1] #  1. Convert the base64 → `PackedVector2Array`
27a20e9c [grok-build-0.1] #  2. Pass that data to the `Node2D`
27a20e9c [grok-build-0.1] #  3. Call `queue_redraw()` on the `Node2D`
27a20e9c [grok-build-0.1] #- The `Node2D` should only draw inside its `_draw()` function.
27a20e9c [grok-build-0.1] #
27a20e9d [grok-build-0.1] #Would you like me to outline the cleanest way to connect these two nodes (e.g. using `@export` or
27a20e9d [grok-build-0.1] #`get_node()`, or signals)?
27a20e9d [grok-build-0.1] #
27a20e9d [grok-build-0.1] #Also, can you share the current content of `node2d.gd`? It's referenced in the scene but I don't
27a20e9e [grok-build-0.1] #have its code yet.
27a20e9e [grok-build-0.1] #
