27a26f37 [grok-build-0.1] #• No, not always.*
27a26f38 [grok-build-0.1] #
27a26f38 [grok-build-0.1] #Current Behavior
27a26f38 [grok-build-0.1] #
27a26f38 [grok-build-0.1] #In your setup, the `log_view` is usually on top, but not because of the `@onready` keyword
27a26f39 [grok-build-0.1] #itself. It's because of child order and how Godot draws things.
27a26f39 [grok-build-0.1] #
27a26f39 [grok-build-0.1] #Here's what's actually happening:
27a26f39 [grok-build-0.1] #
27a26f3a [grok-build-0.1] #
27a26f3a [grok-build-0.1] #@onready var log_view = TextEdit.new()
27a26f3a [grok-build-0.1] #...
27a26f3a [grok-build-0.1] #add_child(log_view)     # This runs in _ready()
27a26f3b [grok-build-0.1] #
27a26f3b [grok-build-0.1] #
27a26f3b [grok-build-0.1] #This adds the `TextEdit` as a child of the `Node` (the networking node).
27a26f3b [grok-build-0.1] #
27a26f3c [grok-build-0.1] #Your current scene hierarchy looks like this:
27a26f3c [grok-build-0.1] #
27a26f3c [grok-build-0.1] #
27a26f3c [grok-build-0.1] #Control
27a26f3d [grok-build-0.1] #├── Node
27a26f3d [grok-build-0.1] #│   └── TextEdit (log_view)     ← Added here
27a26f3d [grok-build-0.1] #└── Node2D
27a26f3d [grok-build-0.1] #
27a26f3e [grok-build-0.1] #
27a26f3e [grok-build-0.1] #Why it usually appears on top:
27a26f3e [grok-build-0.1] #
27a26f3e [grok-build-0.1] #- Godot draws children in the order they appear in the scene tree.
27a26f3f [grok-build-0.1] #- Later siblings are drawn on top of earlier ones.
27a26f3f [grok-build-0.1] #- The `TextEdit` is a `Control`, and the `Node2D` is a `CanvasItem`. When mixed under a `Control`
27a26f3f [grok-build-0.1] #root, the UI element (`TextEdit`) tends to render after custom drawing from `Node2D`.
27a26f3f [grok-build-0.1] #
27a26f40 [grok-build-0.1] #So in practice, the log is currently covering your vector lines.
27a26f40 [grok-build-0.1] #
27a26f40 [grok-build-0.1] #━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━
27a26f40 [grok-build-0.1] #
27a26f41 [grok-build-0.1] #How to Control This
27a26f41 [grok-build-0.1] #
27a26f41 [grok-build-0.1] #Here are your main options, from simplest to better:
27a26f41 [grok-build-0.1] #
27a26f42 [grok-build-0.1] #1. Quick & Dirty (Move the Node2D on top)
27a26f42 [grok-build-0.1] #
27a26f42 [grok-build-0.1] #Add this in the `Node`'s `_ready()`, after adding the log view:
27a26f42 [grok-build-0.1] #
27a26f43 [grok-build-0.1] #
27a26f43 [grok-build-0.1] #func _ready():
27a26f43 [grok-build-0.1] #    ...
27a26f43 [grok-build-0.1] #    add_child(log_view)
27a26f44 [grok-build-0.1] #
27a26f44 [grok-build-0.1] #    # Push the Node2D in front of the log
27a26f44 [grok-build-0.1] #    var node2d = get_node("../Node2D")
27a26f44 [grok-build-0.1] #    node2d.move_to_front()
27a26f45 [grok-build-0.1] #
27a26f45 [grok-build-0.1] #
27a26f45 [grok-build-0.1] #2. Better: Put the log view directly under Control (Recommended)
27a26f45 [grok-build-0.1] #
27a26f46 [grok-build-0.1] #Instead of adding the `TextEdit` to the `Node`, add it to the `Control` root. This gives you more
27a26f46 [grok-build-0.1] #control.
27a26f46 [grok-build-0.1] #
27a26f46 [grok-build-0.1] #Change:
27a26f47 [grok-build-0.1] #
27a26f47 [grok-build-0.1] #add_child(log_view)
27a26f47 [grok-build-0.1] #
27a26f47 [grok-build-0.1] #
27a26f48 [grok-build-0.1] #To:
27a26f48 [grok-build-0.1] #
27a26f48 [grok-build-0.1] #get_parent().add_child(log_view)
27a26f48 [grok-build-0.1] #
27a26f49 [grok-build-0.1] #
27a26f49 [grok-build-0.1] #Then you can use `move_child()` to explicitly control order.
27a26f49 [grok-build-0.1] #
27a26f49 [grok-build-0.1] #3. Use Z-Index (More explicit)
27a26f4a [grok-build-0.1] #
27a26f4a [grok-build-0.1] #On the `Node2D`, you can force it to draw above or below:
27a26f4a [grok-build-0.1] #
27a26f4a [grok-build-0.1] #
27a26f4b [grok-build-0.1] ## In node2d.gd
27a26f4b [grok-build-0.1] #z_index = 10          # Higher = drawn on top
27a26f4b [grok-build-0.1] #
27a26f4b [grok-build-0.1] #
27a26f4c [grok-build-0.1] #Or on the log view:
27a26f4c [grok-build-0.1] #
27a26f4c [grok-build-0.1] #log_view.z_index = 5
27a26f4c [grok-build-0.1] #
27a26f4d [grok-build-0.1] #
27a26f4d [grok-build-0.1] #━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━
27a26f4d [grok-build-0.1] #
27a26f4d [grok-build-0.1] #Quick Question:
27a26f4e [grok-build-0.1] #
27a26f4e [grok-build-0.1] #Do you want the log view on top of the vector graphics (like a HUD), or do you want the
27a26f4e [grok-build-0.1] #vector lines on top of the log?
27a26f4e [grok-build-0.1] #
27a26f4f [grok-build-0.1] #Tell me which one you prefer and I’ll give you the cleanest way to set it up.
27a26f4f [grok-build-0.1] #
