27a3c4b7 [grok-build-0.1] #Realistic Assessment for Serious Games
27a3c4b7 [grok-build-0.1] #
27a3c4b7 [grok-build-0.1] #• Strengths in Godot 4:*
27a3c4b8 [grok-build-0.1] #- Very good performance when mixing 2D and 3D.
27a3c4b8 [grok-build-0.1] #- Easy to use `Node2D` + `Node3D` together (very flexible).
27a3c4b8 [grok-build-0.1] #- Solid 2D tools (TileMap, AnimationPlayer, Sprite2D, etc.) which are often the backbone of 2.5D
27a3c4b8 [grok-build-0.1] #games.
27a3c4b9 [grok-build-0.1] #- Improved 3D lighting and rendering since 4.3 (you’re on 4.7.2, which is recent).
27a3c4b9 [grok-build-0.1] #- Many successful 2.5D-style games have shipped on Steam using Godot.
27a3c4b9 [grok-build-0.1] #
27a3c4b9 [grok-build-0.1] #• Common Challenges:*
27a3c4ba [grok-build-0.1] #- 3D materials and lighting are not as advanced or easy to work with as Unreal Engine.
27a3c4ba [grok-build-0.1] #- Character animation and rigging (especially if using 3D models) is relatively basic.
27a3c4ba [grok-build-0.1] #- If your game needs high-quality 3D environments or complex post-processing, you’ll have to do
27a3c4ba [grok-build-0.1] #more manual work.
27a3c4bb [grok-build-0.1] #- Asset pipeline for 3D is functional but not as polished as Unity or Unreal.
27a3c4bb [grok-build-0.1] #
27a3c4bb [grok-build-0.1] #Recommended Approaches in Godot
27a3c4bb [grok-build-0.1] #
27a3c4bc [grok-build-0.1] #Most people doing serious 2.5D in Godot use one of these methods:
27a3c4bc [grok-build-0.1] #
27a3c4bc [grok-build-0.1] #1. Best for most cases: Use 3D space with 2D sprites (Sprite3D or PlaneMesh + Sprite2D).
27a3c4bd [grok-build-0.1] #This gives you depth, lighting, and parallax while keeping the performance and workflow of 2D.
27a3c4bd [grok-build-0.1] #2. Use an orthographic camera with 3D models (good for games like Hades-style or certain
27a3c4bd [grok-build-0.1] #RPGs).
27a3c4bd [grok-build-0.1] #3. Full 3D with heavy use of 2D elements for UI and effects.
27a3c4be [grok-build-0.1] #
27a3c4be [grok-build-0.1] #Bottom Line for Steam
27a3c4be [grok-build-0.1] #
27a3c4be [grok-build-0.1] #- Small to medium scope 2.5D games: Godot is a solid choice.
27a3c4bf [grok-build-0.1] #- Large scope or very high visual quality: You will likely need more experienced developers
27a3c4bf [grok-build-0.1] #and more time compared to Unreal.
27a3c4bf [grok-build-0.1] #- Steam integration works fine (using the official Steamworks GDExtension).
27a3c4c0 [grok-build-0.1] #
