27c955c5 [gemini-3.8-flash] #Here are a few observations on the updated `snoop.cpp`:
27c955c5 [gemini-3.8-flash] #
27c955c5 [gemini-3.8-flash] #1. FIFO Flush and State Machine Synchronization
27c955c6 [gemini-3.8-flash] #Because `pio_sm_set_enabled(snoop_pio, snoop_sm, true)` is invoked in `initSnoop()`, the state
27c955c6 [gemini-3.8-flash] #machine runs continuously in the background. Prior to calling `beginSnoop()`, any bus transitions
27c955c6 [gemini-3.8-flash] #push words into the RX FIFO.
27c955c6 [gemini-3.8-flash] #
27c955c7 [gemini-3.8-flash] #To ensure the DMA begins reading on an aligned pair boundary (tick first, pins second) rather than
27c955c7 [gemini-3.8-flash] #picking up stale words:
27c955c7 [gemini-3.8-flash] #• Disabling the state machine or draining the FIFO via `pio_sm_clear_fifos(snoop_pio, snoop_sm)`
27c955c7 [gemini-3.8-flash] #right before starting the transfer ensures the FIFO is clean.
27c955c8 [gemini-3.8-flash] #• Restarting or clearing execution state with `pio_sm_restart(snoop_pio, snoop_sm)` and
27c955c8 [gemini-3.8-flash] #`pio_sm_clkdiv_restart(snoop_pio, snoop_sm)` guarantees the PIO routine begins at a known state.
27c955c8 [gemini-3.8-flash] #
27c955c8 [gemini-3.8-flash] #2. Remaining Transfer Truncation in `getCapturedSampleCount`
27c955c9 [gemini-3.8-flash] #In `getCapturedSampleCount()`:
27c955c9 [gemini-3.8-flash] #
27c955c9 [gemini-3.8-flash] #return snoopRequested-(dma_channel_hw_addr(snoop_dma_chan)->transfer_count/2);
27c955ca [gemini-3.8-flash] #
27c955ca [gemini-3.8-flash] #When `stopBusCapture()` is called mid-transfer and an odd number of 32-bit words has arrived, the
27c955ca [gemini-3.8-flash] #integer division rounds in a way that includes the lone half-sample. Computing the completed pairs
27c955ca [gemini-3.8-flash] #from the words transferred avoids reading past valid pairs:
27c955cb [gemini-3.8-flash] #
