27caa089 [gemini-3.8-flash] #🟠nitrologic Relay 2.0.2 gemini-3.8-flash 🌟 🪠 0.7° $0.006 25.36KB 4.47s
27caa089 [gemini-3.8-flash] #In USB CDC-ACM (and TinyUSB's implementation on the RP2040), RTS stands for Request To
27caa089 [gemini-3.8-flash] #Send.
27caa08a [gemini-3.8-flash] #
27caa08a [gemini-3.8-flash] #In the context of `cdcStatus()`:
27caa08a [gemini-3.8-flash] #
27caa08a [gemini-3.8-flash] #1. Virtual Control Line:
27caa08b [gemini-3.8-flash] #   Because native USB does not have physical RS-232 pins, the host driver communicates modern UART
27caa08b [gemini-3.8-flash] #flow-control signals via CDC control packets (`SET_CONTROL_LINE_STATE`). RTS is transmitted as bit
27caa08b [gemini-3.8-flash] #1 of the control line bitmap (bit 0 is DTR, Data Terminal Ready).
27caa08b [gemini-3.8-flash] #
27caa08c [gemini-3.8-flash] #2. Terminal / Host Connection State:
27caa08c [gemini-3.8-flash] #   When a terminal emulator (such as PuTTY, minicom, or a WebUSB serial console) opens the virtual
27caa08c [gemini-3.8-flash] #COM port, it typically asserts DTR and RTS together:
27caa08c [gemini-3.8-flash] #   * DTR (bit 0, value `0x01`): Host terminal indicates it is present and connected.
27caa08d [gemini-3.8-flash] #   * RTS (bit 1, value `0x02`): Host terminal signals it is ready to receive incoming bulk
27caa08d [gemini-3.8-flash] #data from the device.
27caa08d [gemini-3.8-flash] #
27caa08d [gemini-3.8-flash] #3. Status Mask (`status & 3`):
27caa08e [gemini-3.8-flash] #   In your code:
27caa08e [gemini-3.8-flash] #
27caa08e [gemini-3.8-flash] #   int status = cdcStatus();
27caa08e [gemini-3.8-flash] #   if (status & 3) { ... }
27caa08f [gemini-3.8-flash] #
27caa08f [gemini-3.8-flash] #   * A mask of `3` checks both `DTR | RTS` (`0x01 | 0x02`).
27caa08f [gemini-3.8-flash] #   * When `status & 3` evaluates to non-zero, it usually means the USB host has opened the COM port
27caa08f [gemini-3.8-flash] #and signaled that the device is free to stream trace packets over bulk endpoints. When it drops to
27caa090 [gemini-3.8-flash] #`0`, the host serial monitor has closed or disconnected.
27caa090 [gemini-3.8-flash] #
