28090b6d [grok-build-0.1] #Quick summary of what you sent:
28090b6e [grok-build-0.1] #
28090b6e [grok-build-0.1] #- `scrapeschema.gd` — A small runtime scraper that walks `ClassDB`, buckets classes into
28090b6e [grok-build-0.1] #`node`/`resource`/`object`/`editor` categories, collects variant types, and writes a JSON schema.
28090b6e [grok-build-0.1] #- `godotSchema.json.txt` — The output of that scraper (looks like Godot 4.x, with
28090b6f [grok-build-0.1] #`"latest": "4.7.2"`).
28090b6f [grok-build-0.1] #
28090b6f [grok-build-0.1] #Observations
28090b6f [grok-build-0.1] #
28090b70 [grok-build-0.1] #• Positive:*
28090b70 [grok-build-0.1] #- The categorization logic is straightforward and uses `ClassDB.is_parent_class()` correctly.
28090b70 [grok-build-0.1] #- Collecting variants via `type_string()` is a clean way to get the built-in types.
28090b70 [grok-build-0.1] #- Separating `editor` classes is useful if this schema is intended for tooling or documentation.
28090b71 [grok-build-0.1] #- The script is self-contained and quits after running, which is appropriate for a generation tool.
28090b71 [grok-build-0.1] #
28090b71 [grok-build-0.1] #• Things worth noting:*
28090b71 [grok-build-0.1] #
28090b72 [grok-build-0.1] #1. Overlapping categories
28090b72 [grok-build-0.1] #   Many classes appear in both `"node"` (or `"resource"`) and `"object"`. This is expected
28090b72 [grok-build-0.1] #given the inheritance, but depending on how you intend to consume this schema it may or may not be
28090b72 [grok-build-0.1] #desirable.
28090b73 [grok-build-0.1] #
28090b73 [grok-build-0.1] #2. Editor class detection
28090b73 [grok-build-0.1] #   The current check:
28090b73 [grok-build-0.1] #
28090b74 [grok-build-0.1] #   item_name.begins_with("Editor") or item_name.begins_with("ResourceImporter")
28090b74 [grok-build-0.1] #
28090b74 [grok-build-0.1] #   This works for most cases, but can be a bit broad. Some classes like `EditorNode3DGizmoPlugin`
28090b74 [grok-build-0.1] #are correctly caught, but you might eventually want a more precise filter if you start seeing
28090b75 [grok-build-0.1] #noise.
28090b75 [grok-build-0.1] #
28090b75 [grok-build-0.1] #3. Schema metadata
28090b75 [grok-build-0.1] #   The schema version is hardcoded to `"0.1.0"`, while the engine version is pulled dynamically.
28090b76 [grok-build-0.1] #You may want to make the schema version configurable or derive it from something more meaningful.
28090b76 [grok-build-0.1] #
28090b76 [grok-build-0.1] #4. Scope
28090b76 [grok-build-0.1] #   This schema currently only contains class names per category. It does not include:
28090b77 [grok-build-0.1] #   - Inheritance relationships
28090b77 [grok-build-0.1] #   - Methods / signals / properties
28090b77 [grok-build-0.1] #   - Constants
28090b77 [grok-build-0.1] #   - Default values
28090b78 [grok-build-0.1] #
28090b78 [grok-build-0.1] #   If this is meant to be a more complete API surface description, that would be the next logical
28090b78 [grok-build-0.1] #layer.
