2822a0a2 [deepseek-flash] #🟠nitrologic Relay 2.0.3 deepseek-flash 🐋 🪠 0.7° $0.003 945B 13.64s
2822a0a2 [deepseek-flash] #The error is not about JSON syntax. DeepSeek rejected the request because the total prompt is too
2822a0a2 [deepseek-flash] #long for that model’s context window.
2822a0a3 [deepseek-flash] #
2822a0a3 [deepseek-flash] #What is happening:
2822a0a3 [deepseek-flash] #
2822a0a3 [deepseek-flash] #- Your request appears to include a large JSON fragment, likely from Godot’s `extension_api.json`
2822a0a3 [deepseek-flash] #or similar generated API data.
2822a0a4 [deepseek-flash] #- That content is being sent together with chat history and other messages.
2822a0a4 [deepseek-flash] #- DeepSeek counts system prompt + chat history + user message + any file content + reserved output
2822a0a4 [deepseek-flash] #tokens against the model limit.
2822a0a4 [deepseek-flash] #- Code and JSON tokenize poorly, so a file that looks “only a few hundred KB” can easily exceed
2822a0a5 [deepseek-flash] #tens of thousands of tokens.
2822a0a5 [deepseek-flash] #
2822a0a5 [deepseek-flash] #How to fix it:
2822a0a5 [deepseek-flash] #
2822a0a5 [deepseek-flash] #1. Reduce the prompt size.
2822a0a6 [deepseek-flash] #   - Do not send the entire `extension_api.json`.
2822a0a6 [deepseek-flash] #   - Extract only the relevant class, struct, or method. For example, send only the
2822a0a6 [deepseek-flash] #`ScriptLanguageExtensionProfilingInfo` entry and the minimum surrounding context.
2822a0a6 [deepseek-flash] #
2822a0a6 [deepseek-flash] #2. Trim chat history.
2822a0a7 [deepseek-flash] #   - Keep only the most recent relevant messages.
2822a0a7 [deepseek-flash] #   - Remove earlier large assistant outputs or duplicated file contents.
2822a0a7 [deepseek-flash] #
2822a0a7 [deepseek-flash] #3. Lower `max_tokens` if the API counts it toward the context limit.
2822a0a7 [deepseek-flash] #   - Some providers require `prompt tokens + max_tokens <= context window`.
2822a0a8 [deepseek-flash] #   - If `max_tokens` is very high, it leaves less room for the prompt.
2822a0a8 [deepseek-flash] #
2822a0a8 [deepseek-flash] #4. Use a model with a larger context window.
2822a0a9 [deepseek-flash] #   - If DeepSeek’s limit is smaller than other models you are testing, switch models or reduce
2822a0a9 [deepseek-flash] #input before comparing.
2822a0a9 [deepseek-flash] #
2822a0a9 [deepseek-flash] #5. Chunk the file.
2822a0a9 [deepseek-flash] #   - Split the JSON into sections, process each section separately, then combine the results.
2822a0a9 [deepseek-flash] #   - Or use retrieval/search so only relevant chunks are sent.
2822a0aa [deepseek-flash] #
2822a0aa [deepseek-flash] #6. Minify and filter.
2822a0aa [deepseek-flash] #   - Remove whitespace, descriptions, default values, and unrelated classes if they are not needed.
2822a0aa [deepseek-flash] #   - Send the smallest valid JSON object that answers the question.
2822a0aa [deepseek-flash] #
2822a0aa [deepseek-flash] #7. Check token count before sending.
2822a0ab [deepseek-flash] #   - Do not estimate from character count alone. Use the model’s tokenizer or an API token-count
2822a0ab [deepseek-flash] #endpoint if available.
2822a0ab [deepseek-flash] #
2822a0ab [deepseek-flash] #8. Check your router or wrapper.
2822a0ac [deepseek-flash] #   - If you are using an API router, make sure it is not prepending a large system prompt or
2822a0ac [deepseek-flash] #duplicating the conversation history.
2822a0ac [deepseek-flash] #
2822a0ac [deepseek-flash] #If you tell me which DeepSeek model you are calling, the approximate size of the JSON you are
2822a0ad [deepseek-flash] #sending, and whether you can reduce it to just the `ScriptLanguageExtensionProfilingInfo` section,
2822a0ad [deepseek-flash] #I can suggest a more specific trim strategy.
2822a0ad [deepseek-flash] #
