28238235 [deepseek-flash] #Issues
28238235 [deepseek-flash] #
28238236 [deepseek-flash] #1. `onFrame` arity mismatch — declared as `func onFrame(client, packet)`, called with three
28238236 [deepseek-flash] #args. This will error the moment a frame arrives. Should be `func onFrame(client, header:
28238236 [deepseek-flash] #Dictionary, binary: PackedByteArray)`.
28238236 [deepseek-flash] #
28238237 [deepseek-flash] #2. `out.fill()` fills the entire buffer — `PackedByteArray.fill()` defaults to `0..size()`.
28238237 [deepseek-flash] #Both `out.fill(0x20)` and `out.fill(0x00)` wipe the magic, version, length, and chunk headers you
28238237 [deepseek-flash] #just wrote. `fill()` needs explicit ranges: `out.fill(0x20, 20 + json.size(), 20 + json_len)` and
28238237 [deepseek-flash] #`out.fill(0x00, 28 + json_len + binary.size(), out.size())`.
28238238 [deepseek-flash] #
28238238 [deepseek-flash] #3. JSON body is never copied into `out` — `build_frame` writes the JSON chunk header but
28238238 [deepseek-flash] #not `json` itself. Same for the BIN chunk. Simplest fix is to build by concatenation instead of
28238238 [deepseek-flash] #pre-sizing and filling:
28238239 [deepseek-flash] #
