2823c995 [deepseek-flash] #That’s just missing export templates — Godot doesn’t ship them with the editor. The version in the
2823c996 [deepseek-flash] #path must match the editor exactly (`4.7.2.stable`), so a template for `4.7.1` or `4.7.3` won’t be
2823c996 [deepseek-flash] #picked up.
2823c996 [deepseek-flash] #
2823c996 [deepseek-flash] #Three ways to fix it:
2823c997 [deepseek-flash] #
2823c997 [deepseek-flash] #• 1. Editor (normal path)*
2823c997 [deepseek-flash] #- `Editor → Manage Export Templates…`
2823c997 [deepseek-flash] #- Click Download and Install
2823c998 [deepseek-flash] #- If the download fails or 4.7.2 isn’t listed yet, use option 2.
2823c998 [deepseek-flash] #
2823c998 [deepseek-flash] #• 2. Manual install*
2823c999 [deepseek-flash] #- Grab the matching `.tpz` from https://github.com/godotengine/godot/releases (look for
2823c999 [deepseek-flash] #`Godot_v4.7.2-stable_export_templates.tpz`).
2823c999 [deepseek-flash] #- In the same Manage Export Templates dialog, click Install from File… and point it at the
2823c999 [deepseek-flash] #`.tpz`.
2823c99a [deepseek-flash] #
2823c99a [deepseek-flash] #• 3. Manual extraction (if the dialog is uncooperative)*
2823c99a [deepseek-flash] #- Rename the `.tpz` to `.zip` and extract.
2823c99a [deepseek-flash] #- You’ll get a `templates/` folder. Copy its contents into:
2823c99b [deepseek-flash] #
2823c99b [deepseek-flash] #  C:\Users\nitro\AppData\Roaming\Godot\export_templates\4.7.2.stable\
2823c99b [deepseek-flash] #
2823c99b [deepseek-flash] #- The folder should end up containing `windows_debug_x86_64.exe`, `windows_release_x86_64.exe`,
2823c99c [deepseek-flash] #`version.txt`, etc.
2823c99c [deepseek-flash] #
2823c99c [deepseek-flash] #A couple of gotchas worth checking before you chase the download:
2823c99c [deepseek-flash] #
2823c99d [deepseek-flash] #- Run `godot --version` (or check Help → About) and confirm it really is `4.7.2.stable`. If it’s
2823c99d [deepseek-flash] #e.g. `4.7.2.rc1` or `4.7.2.stable.mono`, the template folder name differs.
2823c99d [deepseek-flash] #- If you’re on the .NET/Mono build, you need the Mono export templates, not the standard ones.
