2823e10e [grok-build-0.1] #• Files received and reviewed.*
2823e10e [grok-build-0.1] #
2823e10f [grok-build-0.1] #Here's a clean summary of what you've shared:
2823e10f [grok-build-0.1] #
2823e10f [grok-build-0.1] #Overview
2823e10f [grok-build-0.1] #This is a Godot relay/host project (`nitrologic`) that bridges Godot with an external
2823e110 [grok-build-0.1] #system. It runs two roles simultaneously:
2823e110 [grok-build-0.1] #- Server: TCP port 8080 (accepting WebSocket connections from local clients)
2823e110 [grok-build-0.1] #- Client: Connects upstream to `ws://localhost:9000`
2823e110 [grok-build-0.1] #
2823e111 [grok-build-0.1] #It uses a custom binary framing protocol (`NTRL` magic) that carries a JSON header + optional
2823e111 [grok-build-0.1] #binary payload.
2823e111 [grok-build-0.1] #
2823e111 [grok-build-0.1] #Key Components
2823e112 [grok-build-0.1] #
2823e112 [grok-build-0.1] #╭────────────────────────────────┬─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────╮
2823e112 [grok-build-0.1] #│  File                          │  Purpose                                                                                                                                                │
2823e112 [grok-build-0.1] #├────────────────────────────────┼─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤
2823e113 [grok-build-0.1] #│  `node.gd`                     │  Core networking + protocol logic. Handles frame building/parsing, TCP server, upstream WebSocket, command dispatch (`snoop`, `init`, `draw`, `tick`).  │
2823e113 [grok-build-0.1] #│  `node2d.gd`                   │  Simple 2D line renderer. Receives `PackedVector2Array` and draws via `draw_multiline`.                                                                 │
2823e113 [grok-build-0.1] #│  `snoop.gd`                    │  Godot ClassDB introspection. Builds a schema of classes and their methods.                                                                             │
2823e114 [grok-build-0.1] #│  `control.gd`                  │  Minimal UI host (just prints on ready).                                                                                                                │
2823e114 [grok-build-0.1] #│  `extension_api.json` snippet  │  Context about `VisualShaderNodeTransformParameter` (uniform mat4).                                                                                     │
2823e114 [grok-build-0.1] #╰────────────────────────────────┴─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────╯
2823e114 [grok-build-0.1] #
2823e114 [grok-build-0.1] #Notable Design Points
2823e115 [grok-build-0.1] #
2823e115 [grok-build-0.1] #• Protocol*
2823e115 [grok-build-0.1] #- Custom framed format with 4-byte alignment padding.
2823e116 [grok-build-0.1] #- JSON chunk (`JSON`) + binary chunk (`BIN\0`).
2823e116 [grok-build-0.1] #- The `onBuffer` path stores binary data by name in a global dictionary (separate from the JSON
2823e116 [grok-build-0.1] #command path).
2823e116 [grok-build-0.1] #
2823e117 [grok-build-0.1] #• Commands currently handled*
2823e117 [grok-build-0.1] #- `snoop` — triggers schema dump via the Snoop node
2823e117 [grok-build-0.1] #- `init` — sends splash screen geometry to the Node2D
2823e117 [grok-build-0.1] #- `draw` — accepts base64-encoded float32 vec2 pairs and updates the line renderer
2823e118 [grok-build-0.1] #- `tick` — currently just logs
2823e118 [grok-build-0.1] #
2823e118 [grok-build-0.1] #• Introspection*
2823e118 [grok-build-0.1] #The `snoop.gd` implementation walks `ClassDB` and builds a dictionary of class → method names. A
2823e119 [grok-build-0.1] #lot of the richer metadata (arguments, return types, categories) is currently commented out or only
2823e119 [grok-build-0.1] #partially populated.
2823e119 [grok-build-0.1] #
2823e119 [grok-build-0.1] #Observations
2823e11a [grok-build-0.1] #
2823e11a [grok-build-0.1] #1. Networking is all polled in `_process`. This works but will become noisy as traffic
2823e11a [grok-build-0.1] #grows. The current split between framed binary and plain text packets is handled reasonably.
2823e11a [grok-build-0.1] #
2823e11b [grok-build-0.1] #2. The `base64_to_vec2_array` function makes a strong assumption about the incoming format (tightly
2823e11b [grok-build-0.1] #packed float32 pairs). This is fragile if the external side ever changes encoding.
2823e11b [grok-build-0.1] #
2823e11b [grok-build-0.1] #3. The splash screen and draw paths both end up feeding the same `Node2D.set_lines()` method — the
2823e11c [grok-build-0.1] #architecture is starting to show a "remote drawing" use case.
2823e11c [grok-build-0.1] #
2823e11c [grok-build-0.1] #4. `snoop` currently only emits method names. If the external consumer needs signatures, argument
2823e11c [grok-build-0.1] #types, or property information, the current schema is quite limited.
2823e11d [grok-build-0.1] #
2823e11d [grok-build-0.1] #━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━
2823e11d [grok-build-0.1] #
