287686cc [deepseek-flash] #A few observations on this one:
287686cc [deepseek-flash] #
287686cc [deepseek-flash] #• What's accurate and well-chosen*
287686cd [deepseek-flash] #- Highland Park, Illinois is correct, and the peers list is defensible: Lessig was a mentor and
287686cd [deepseek-flash] #Creative Commons collaborator; Berners-Lee connects through the W3C RDF Core Working Group and the
287686cd [deepseek-flash] #Semantic Web work.
287686cd [deepseek-flash] #- The two ethos topics are a good compression of his arc — RSS 1.0 is protocol design, and the
287686ce [deepseek-flash] #JSTOR/Open Access work is information access. They're the through-line rather than just a list of
287686ce [deepseek-flash] #projects.
287686ce [deepseek-flash] #- Dates check out: 8 November 1986, 11 January 2013.
287686ce [deepseek-flash] #
287686cf [deepseek-flash] #• What's new or different here (versus a typical bio blurb)*
287686cf [deepseek-flash] #- Structuring the person as `ethos` + `journey` rather than a prose paragraph is the interesting
287686cf [deepseek-flash] #move — it forces the biography to declare a thesis rather than recite a résumé.
287686cf [deepseek-flash] #- `credits` as an array with a model listed alongside a human author is notable metadata. It's
287686d0 [deepseek-flash] #honest, but it also means the file format itself has to be able to express "who made this" when the
287686d0 [deepseek-flash] #answer is mixed.
287686d0 [deepseek-flash] #- The description ("knee deep in RSS and open systems") is deliberately informal. Given the rest of
287686d0 [deepseek-flash] #the schema is tidy and structured, the tone reads as a deliberate counterweight rather than an
287686d1 [deepseek-flash] #oversight — though it's the one line that would look out of place if this file is ever rendered
287686d1 [deepseek-flash] #next to, say, a Kant entry.
287686d1 [deepseek-flash] #
287686d1 [deepseek-flash] #• Things I'd flag*
287686d2 [deepseek-flash] #- MIT is a software license. Applying it to a biographical record is unusual — worth deciding
287686d2 [deepseek-flash] #whether `license` here means the file, the schema, or the content, because
287686d2 [deepseek-flash] #those have different answers and a reader may assume the wrong one.
287686d2 [deepseek-flash] #- `version: 0.1` plus a single copyright year suggests this schema is early. If entries will
287686d3 [deepseek-flash] #eventually be cross-referenced by `peers`, those strings will need to resolve to other files
287686d3 [deepseek-flash] #(Berners-Lee, Lessig) — otherwise they're just text and the graph doesn't close.
287686d3 [deepseek-flash] #- Minor: `topics` has a trailing space after `"Protocol Design", ` — harmless, but if anything
287686d3 [deepseek-flash] #downstream diffs these strings it'll matter.
287686d4 [deepseek-flash] #
287686d4 [deepseek-flash] #Is the intent that `peers` become links into other entries in `books/biography/`, or are they free
287686d4 [deepseek-flash] #text on purpose?
287686d4 [deepseek-flash] #
