28769021 [deepseek-flash] #🟠nitrologic Relay 2.0.3 deepseek-flash 🐋 🪠 0.7° $0.020 83.40KB 65.99s
28769022 [deepseek-flash] #A few notes, split between what's distinctive and what looks like it needs a second pass.
28769022 [deepseek-flash] #
28769022 [deepseek-flash] #• The design pattern that's actually new*
28769022 [deepseek-flash] #The self-referential bits are the interesting move here. `symbol` ✴ reappears inside
28769023 [deepseek-flash] #`fenced.code.starChars`; `separator` (the five fish) has a matching `unicode.lexis."𓆛𓆟"` entry
28769023 [deepseek-flash] #named "Fish 1"; `motto` is Coptic and Coptic gets its own `spec.coptic` block. The metadata is
28769023 [deepseek-flash] #written in the scripts the file catalogues. That's a deliberate loop, not decoration.
28769023 [deepseek-flash] #
28769024 [deepseek-flash] #Also different from a typical spec file:
28769024 [deepseek-flash] #- `pheme` is a compositional generator (prefixes × suffixes), not a flat vocabulary list.
28769024 [deepseek-flash] #- `orient` is a list of reference-point definitions with a recurring refrain ("reference for…"),
28769025 [deepseek-flash] #which reads as an essay in a data structure.
28769025 [deepseek-flash] #- `systemic fails` is poetic register ("a recursive push decrements pointer to no return") sitting
28769025 [deepseek-flash] #alongside technical tables.
28769025 [deepseek-flash] #- The `schema`/`types` block at the end only covers `relay` and `PathItem`. Everything else —
28769025 [deepseek-flash] #Unicode, food, cables, geography — is unvalidated. The schema is the smallest part of a very large
28769026 [deepseek-flash] #document.
28769026 [deepseek-flash] #
28769026 [deepseek-flash] #• Things that look wrong*
28769026 [deepseek-flash] #1. `spec.coptic.alphabet` — both `upper` and `lower` omit Ⲭ/ⲭ (khi). Standard order runs Ⲫ Ⲭ Ⲯ Ⲱ.
28769026 [deepseek-flash] #2. `spec.pheme.pre61.body12` has 11 items, not 12.
28769027 [deepseek-flash] #3. `spec.shortcode`:
28769027 [deepseek-flash] #   - `"lime":"🫒"` — 🫒 is OLIVE.
28769027 [deepseek-flash] #   - `"shovel":"🫷"` — 🫷 is RIGHTWARDS PUSHING HAND; shovel is 🪏.
28769027 [deepseek-flash] #   - `"phoenix":"🪶"` — 🪶 is FEATHER; phoenix is 🐦‍🔥, which appears correctly in
28769028 [deepseek-flash] #`fenced.code.birds`.
28769028 [deepseek-flash] #4. `spec.technology.virtualkeys` appears to skip `VK_PACKET` (0xE7) and its 0xE8 placeholder.
28769028 [deepseek-flash] #5. `spec.encoding.riff` — the key `"CC"` is odd for the INFO chunk; `"INFO"` (or `"I-*"`) would
28769028 [deepseek-flash] #match the source.
28769029 [deepseek-flash] #6. `spec.unicode.lexis."㊊㊐"` is ordered by code point (Moon, Fire, Water, Wood, Metal, Earth, Sun),
28769029 [deepseek-flash] #not by the traditional Wu Xing cycle.
28769029 [deepseek-flash] #7. `spec.digits` — the CJK entry is 11 characters (includes 十), all others are 10. "Roman" also
28769029 [deepseek-flash] #sits oddly beside 0–9 sets since it has no zero.
2876902a [deepseek-flash] #
2876902a [deepseek-flash] #• Softer flags*
2876902a [deepseek-flash] #- `ambiguousstates` mixes genuinely contested cases (Kosovo, Western Sahara) with uncontested ones
2876902a [deepseek-flash] #(Singapore, Monaco) and internal regions (Tibet, Hong Kong, Macau), and assigns "Russia" as `rule`
2876902a [deepseek-flash] #for Abkhazia/South Ossetia/Transnistria. The category name doesn't fit all of it.
2876902b [deepseek-flash] #- `spec.food` — Dosa appears in both `flatbread` and `pancake`; Msemen appears in flatbread plus
2876902b [deepseek-flash] #"Msemen (with batter variant)" in pancake. If these lists are meant to be disjoint, they aren't.
2876902b [deepseek-flash] #- `identifier.msdos` uses a colon (`name:ext`) where 8.3 conventionally uses a dot. Since the same
2876902b [deepseek-flash] #file uses colon as an identifier-type separator (`wikidata:Q42`), that will collide.
2876902c [deepseek-flash] #- `scales.blues` has numerals/degrees/intervals but no solfege, unlike `major`. Probably
2876902c [deepseek-flash] #intentional, but worth confirming.
2876902c [deepseek-flash] #- `unicode.lexis."∧⊽"` is tagged `Sm`, but ↑/↓ (U+2191/2193) are So.
2876902c [deepseek-flash] #- `numbers.dots` and `numbers.holes` are two variants of the same negative-circled family (sans vs
2876902d [deepseek-flash] #serif); "dots" is the weaker of the two names.
2876902d [deepseek-flash] #- `internet.pipes` concatenates names ("LosAngelesUS") while `internet.zones` uses "@region" syntax
2876902d [deepseek-flash] #— two conventions for the same kind of data.
2876902d [deepseek-flash] #
2876902e [deepseek-flash] #Is `spec` intended to eventually be validated against the `schema` block, or is the schema there
2876902e [deepseek-flash] #only for `relay`?
2876902e [deepseek-flash] #
